n":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T02:01:32Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T02:01:32Z","body":"> It causes problems when translating addons, because any translation injected to editor's domains have to be re-added, which is rather problematic\r\n\r\nJust to be clear. Addon translations are intended to use their own translation domain rather than injecting the editor's domain. `godot.*` domains are reserved.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5433413100/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5438129700","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122736#issuecomment-5438129700","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122736","id":5438129700,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRCNGJA","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T11:10:18Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T11:10:18Z","body":"> Addon translations are intended to use their own translation domain rather than injecting the editor's domain.\r\n\r\nIs there an easy way to copy translations from editor's domain to the custom one? Otherwise by assigning custom domain you lose access to many strings that are already translated, and especially the builtin nodes like EditorFileDialog will not be translated, unless you duplicate their translations.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5438129700/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5439520588","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122736#issuecomment-5439520588","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122736","id":5439520588,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRDh_TA","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T13:02:25Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T13:02:25Z","body":"@KoBeWi There is currently no such way I think. But users can set a certain node's translation domain to `godot.editor` if they do want to reuse editor's translations (not recommended though).\r\n\r\nBuiltin `Editor*` nodes should be using the `godot.editor` translation domain explicitly so users don't have to set anything.\r\n\r\ne.g., `EditorFileDialog` does this at least in 4.4 (the demo project in #95787 shows this as a feature). The code was probably lost during some later refactoring.\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/21ca54848989635cbe3452dfed811c1914d09baa/editor/gui/editor_file_dialog.cpp#L253-L255","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5439520588/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5439598051","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122736#issuecomment-5439598051","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122736","id":5439598051,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRDmt4w","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-27T13:09:11Z","updated_at":"2026-08-27T13:09:11Z","body":"There are also non-editor nodes, like AcceptDialog, that use extractable translation (which is part of `godot.editor`).\r\n\r\n> There is currently no such way I think. But users can set a certain node's translation domain to godot.editor if they do want to reuse editor's translations (not recommended though).\r\n\r\nSetting it for each relevant node sounds like a hassle. I use `godot.editor` injecting, because it's very easy to setup and requires no scene changes at all.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5439598051/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5447457474","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122736#issuecomment-5447457474","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122736","id":5447457474,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABRLGawg","user":{"login":"timothyqiu","id":372476,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3MjQ3Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/372476?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu","html_url":"https://github.com/timothyqiu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/timothyqiu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-28T01:59:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-28T02:01:42Z","body":"I agree with your concern, but I'd argue that injection is a hack that shouldn't be encouraged, despite its convenience.\r\n\r\nThere are some problems with injection, e.g.,\r\n\r\n- Can't override existing translations (context can be used as a workaround though)\r\n- If an editor string changes or disappears, your plugin's translation breaks silently\r\n- There's no clear ownership or responsibility boundary\r\n\r\nPOT templates for plugin translations can be generated the same way as for a game project. Extractable strings can also be automatically added to the template.\r\n\r\nYes, with this approach, plugins have to manually translate extractable strings. We can't currently reuse translations already in the editor's domain. This is inconvenient, but it's a limitation of our translation system in general. Game \r\nprojects face the same problem.\r\n\r\nTherefore, I think we should keep this friction intentional. It motivates improvements to the translation infrastructure and benefits both game projects and plugins. Rather than providing shortcuts for injection / setting translation domains, we should focus on solving the real limitation: how to make existing extractable translations available for reuse. (e.g., allow saving extractable translations for certain languages as `.po` / `.csv` files)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5447457474/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6265217955","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122736#issuecomment-6265217955","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122736","id":6265217955,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABdW-jow","user":{"login":"KoBeWi","id":2223172,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyMjMxNzI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi","html_url":"https://github.com/KoBeWi","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KoBeWi/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-19T10:34:22Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T10:34:22Z","body":"> Yes, with this approach, plugins have to manually translate extractable strings. We can't currently reuse translations already in the editor's domain. This is inconvenient, but it's a limitation of our translation system in general. Game\r\nprojects face the same problem.\r\n\r\nI guess #122927 could be a solution. The only problem is that the translation is duplicated inside the plugin and can become outdated.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6265217955/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]